hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"159601","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu Layla ibn Abdullah ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Sahl from Sahl ibn Abi Hathma that some of the great men of his people informed him that Abdullah ibn Sahl and Muhayyisa went out to Khaybar because extreme poverty had overtaken them. Muhayyisa returned and said that Abdullah ibn Sahl had been killed and thrown in a shallow well or spring. The jews came and he said"
"159602","Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu Layla ibn Abdullah ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Sahl from Sahl ibn Abi Hathma that some of the great men of his people informed him that Abdullah ibn Sahl and Muhayyisa went out to Khaybar because extreme poverty had overtaken them. Muhayyisa returned and said that Abdullah ibn Sahl had been killed and thrown in a shallow well or spring. The jews came and he said"
"159701","[1597] Malik told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, that he said: I heard Abu al-Hubab Saeed bin Yassar say: I heard Abu Hurairah says: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: I was ordered to eat villages. They say: Yathrib, but there it is. Medina expels people just as a kiln expels iron slag.\\nMutta Imam Malik Hadith: 1597 Arabic Hadith:"
"159702","[1597] Malik told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, that he said: I heard Abu al-Hubab Saeed bin Yassar say: I heard Abu Hurairah says: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: I was ordered to eat villages. They say: Yathrib, but there it is. Medina expels people just as a kiln expels iron slag.\\nMutta Imam Malik Hadith: 1597 Arabic Hadith:"
